# Copy this file to .env and fill in the two values below:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Both come from the Supabase dashboard: Project Settings -> API. They are the
# same two already set on the deployment, so you can also copy them out of
# Vercel: Project Settings -> Environment Variables.
#
# .env is git-ignored. Keep it that way — not because these values are secret
# (see the note under the anon key) but because your .env is yours.

# Project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijklmnop.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# The "anon public" key — the long one labelled anon, NOT the service_role key.
#
# This one is meant to be public: Vite inlines it into the JavaScript bundle
# that every visitor downloads, so it cannot be hidden and is not trying to be.
# What protects the data is row-level security — every policy in
# supabase/schema.sql is granted `to authenticated`, so the key alone reads
# nothing without a real sign-in.
#
# The service_role key is the opposite: it bypasses row-level security
# entirely. It must never go in this file, or anywhere else in this repository.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
